// expect: compile_error
// expect-error: E300

// GAP — owner: 0.0.8, the same boundary as B2.
// Measured 2026-09-11: two error[E300] Argument Type Mismatch.
//
// `fst` works perfectly at one tuple shape — see
// ../../working/accepts/project_tuple_known_shape.flx. What it cannot do is
// serve two.
//
// The reason is that a field or tuple predicate *pins* its receiver rather
// than quantifying it. `decide_quantification` removes the receiver's
// variables from the quantifiable set, precisely so that a binding cannot go
// polymorphic over a receiver nothing can determine — because a quantified
// receiver's predicate is discharged nowhere, and the `E490` that should be
// reported at the access is silently lost. That was the failure mode the first
// attempt at widening generalization hit.
//
// So the pin is not an oversight; it is what makes the error reportable. The
// cost is this file: the first call site determines the receiver, and the
// second disagrees with it.

fn fst(p) { p.0 }

fn main() with IO {
    print(fst((1, 2)))
    print(fst(("a", true)))
}
